-          "quote": "Let $U,V$ be as in [[def-regular-minimum-energy-path-in-a-collision-free-tube]]. **Inputs:** $x_0\\in U$, a unit vector $v_0$, finite-difference distance $\\epsilon>0$, force-evaluation error bound $\\eta\\ge0$, rotation step $\\alpha>0$, rotation tolerance $\\tau_{\\rm rot}\\ge0$, force tolerance $\\tau_F\\ge0$, rotation cap $J\\in\\mathbb N_0$, translation step $\\sigma>0$, and translation cap $K\\in\\mathbb N_0$. Return the last point, direction, reported residuals, and a status from `force-tolerance`, `mode-unverified`, `rotation-cap`, `translation-cap`, `geometry-failure`, `rotation-failure`, or `nonfinite-evaluation`.\n\nAt each translation iteration, start with the current unit direction $v$. For at most $J$ rotations:\n\n1. If $x\\pm\\epsilon v\\notin U$, return `geometry-failure`. Evaluate approximate gradients $\\widehat g_\\pm$ at $x\\pm\\epsilon v$ with the declared error bound, and form $D_\\epsilon=(\\widehat g_+-\\widehat g_-)/(2\\epsilon)$. Nonfinite data return `nonfinite-evaluation`.\n2. Set $r_{\\rm rot}=\\|(I-vv^T)D_\\epsilon\\|_2$. If $r_{\\rm rot}\\le\\tau_{\\rm rot}$, end this rotation loop. Otherwise set $w=v-\\alpha(I-vv^T)D_\\epsilon$. If $w=0$, return `rotation-failure`; else replace $v$ by $w/\\|w\\|_2$.\n\nIf the rotation cap is reached before the residual test succeeds, return `rotation-cap` with the last direction. A small rotational residual by itself does not certify that the direction is the lowest eigenmode. If no validated spectral-gap or mode-tracking certificate is supplied, label the mode status `mode-unverified`.\n\nAfter a rotation residual passes, evaluate $\\widehat g(x)$ with error at most $\\eta$. If it is nonfinite, return `nonfinite-evaluation`. If $\\|\\widehat g(x)\\|_2\\le\\tau_F$, return `force-tolerance` together with the mode status. If the translation cap has been reached, return `translation-cap`. Otherwise update\n\n$$x^+=x+\\sigma\\bigl[-\\widehat g(x)+2(\\widehat g(x)^Tv)v\\bigr].$$\n\nIf $x^+\\notin U$, return `geometry-failure`; otherwise set $x\\leftarrow x^+$ and repeat. This finite procedure makes no arbitrary-start, termination, saddle-convergence, or global-transition claim.",
+          "quote": "Let $U,V$ be as in [[def-regular-minimum-energy-path-in-a-collision-free-tube]]. **Inputs:** $x_0\\in U$, a unit vector $v_0$, finite-difference distance $\\epsilon>0$, force-evaluation error bound $\\eta\\ge0$, rotation step $\\alpha>0$, rotation tolerance $\\tau_{\\rm rot}\\ge0$, force tolerance $\\tau_F\\ge0$, rotation cap $J\\in\\mathbb N_0$, translation step $\\sigma>0$, and translation cap $K\\in\\mathbb N_0$. Return the last point, direction, reported residuals, and a status from `force-tolerance`, `mode-unverified`, `rotation-cap`, `translation-cap`, `geometry-failure`, `rotation-failure`, or `nonfinite-evaluation`.\n\nInitialize the translation-update counter $k=0$, the current point $x=x_0$, and the current unit direction $v=v_0$. At each translation iteration, start with the current $v$, set the rotation-update counter $j=0$, and repeat the following residual test and possible update:\n\n1. If $x\\pm\\epsilon v\\notin U$, return `geometry-failure`. Evaluate approximate gradients $\\widehat g_\\pm$ at $x\\pm\\epsilon v$ with the declared error bound, and form $D_\\epsilon=(\\widehat g_+-\\widehat g_-)/(2\\epsilon)$. Nonfinite data return `nonfinite-evaluation`.\n2. Set $r_{\\rm rot}=\\|(I-vv^T)D_\\epsilon\\|_2$. If $r_{\\rm rot}\\le\\tau_{\\rm rot}$, end this rotation loop. If the test fails and $j=J$, return `rotation-cap` with the last direction. Otherwise set $w=v-\\alpha(I-vv^T)D_\\epsilon$. If $w=0$, return `rotation-failure`; else replace $v$ by $w/\\|w\\|_2$, set $j\\leftarrow j+1$, and repeat the rotation test.\n\nThus $J$ counts direction updates, and the current direction is tested before the cap is returned, including when $J=0$. A small rotational residual by itself does not certify that the direction is the lowest eigenmode. If no validated spectral-gap or mode-tracking certificate is supplied, label the mode status `mode-unverified`.\n\nAfter a rotation residual passes, evaluate $\\widehat g(x)$ with error at most $\\eta$. If it is nonfinite, return `nonfinite-evaluation`. If $\\|\\widehat g(x)\\|_2\\le\\tau_F$, return `force-tolerance` together with the mode status. If $k=K$, return `translation-cap`; perform an update only when $k<K$.\n\n$$x^+=x+\\sigma\\bigl[-\\widehat g(x)+2(\\widehat g(x)^Tv)v\\bigr].$$\n\nIf $x^+\\notin U$, return `geometry-failure`; otherwise set $x\\leftarrow x^+$, set $k\\leftarrow k+1$, and begin the next translation iteration. Thus $K$ counts translation updates; the force-tolerance test is made before the cap test, including when $K=0$. This finite procedure makes no arbitrary-start, termination, saddle-convergence, or global-transition claim.",
