-          "quote": "Let $U,V,a,b$ satisfy [[def-regular-minimum-energy-path-in-a-collision-free-tube]]. **Inputs:** an integer $M\\ge2$, images $R_0=a,R_1,\\ldots,R_M=b$ in $U$, spring constant $k\\ge0$, fixed step $\\eta>0$, force and spacing tolerances $\\tau_F,\\tau_s\\ge0$, an ordinary-step count $n_{\\rm climb}\\in\\mathbb N_0$, and a finite update budget $N\\in\\mathbb N_0$. Require $n_{\\rm climb}\\le N$. **Output:** the last chain and one of `tolerances-met`, `tangent-failure`, `geometry-failure`, `nonfinite-evaluation`, or `budget-exhausted`.\n\nAt each iteration, endpoints are fixed and only interior images are updated. For $i=1,\\ldots,M-1$, write $\\Delta_i^+=R_{i+1}-R_i$, $\\Delta_i^-=R_i-R_{i-1}$, and $V_i=V(R_i)$. Select an unnormalized tangent by\n\n$$\\tau_i=\\begin{cases}\\Delta_i^+,&V_{i+1}>V_i>V_{i-1},\\\\\\Delta_i^-,&V_{i+1}<V_i<V_{i-1},\\\\w_{\\max}\\Delta_i^+ + w_{\\min}\\Delta_i^-,&\\text{otherwise and }V_{i+1}>V_{i-1},\\\\w_{\\min}\\Delta_i^+ + w_{\\max}\\Delta_i^-,&\\text{otherwise and }V_{i+1}<V_{i-1},\\\\\\Delta_i^++\\Delta_i^-,&V_{i+1}=V_{i-1},\\end{cases}$$\n\nwhere $w_{\\max}=\\max(|V_{i+1}-V_i|,|V_{i-1}-V_i|)$ and $w_{\\min}=\\min(|V_{i+1}-V_i|,|V_{i-1}-V_i|)$. If $\\tau_i=0$, return `tangent-failure`; otherwise set $t_i=\\tau_i/\\|\\tau_i\\|_2$. Nonfinite energies, gradients, or forces return `nonfinite-evaluation`.\n\nBefore iteration $n_{\\rm climb}$, use the ordinary force\n\n$$F_i=-(I-t_it_i^T)\\nabla V(R_i)+k(\\|\\Delta_i^+\\|_2-\\|\\Delta_i^-\\|_2)t_i.$$\n\nStarting at iteration $n_{\\rm climb}$, choose the least index $i_*$ attaining the largest interior energy and replace that image's force by\n\n$$F_{i_*}^{\\rm CI}=-\\nabla V(R_{i_*})+2(\\nabla V(R_{i_*})^Tt_{i_*})t_{i_*};$$\n\nthe climbing image has no spring force. The remaining interior images retain the ordinary force. At each iteration report the maximum force norm and spacing residual $\\max_i|\\|\\Delta_i^+\\|_2-\\|\\Delta_i^-\\|_2|$. Stop with `tolerances-met` only if both are within their declared tolerances. If the budget is exhausted first, return `budget-exhausted`. Otherwise update every interior image by $R_i^{k+1}=R_i^k+\\eta F_i^k$; leaving $U$ returns `geometry-failure`.\n\nThe finite stopping status does not assert convergence to a MEP, a saddle, or a continuum path.",
+          "quote": "Let $U,V,a,b$ satisfy [[def-regular-minimum-energy-path-in-a-collision-free-tube]]. **Inputs:** an integer $M\\ge2$, images $R_0=a,R_1,\\ldots,R_M=b$ in $U$, spring constant $\\kappa\\ge0$, fixed step $\\eta>0$, force and spacing tolerances $\\tau_F,\\tau_s\\ge0$, an ordinary-step count $n_{\\rm climb}\\in\\mathbb N_0$, and a finite update budget $N\\in\\mathbb N_0$. Require $n_{\\rm climb}\\le N$. **Output:** the last chain and one of `tolerances-met`, `tangent-failure`, `geometry-failure`, `nonfinite-evaluation`, or `budget-exhausted`.\n\nAt each iteration, endpoints are fixed and only interior images are updated. For $i=1,\\ldots,M-1$, write $\\Delta_i^+=R_{i+1}-R_i$, $\\Delta_i^-=R_i-R_{i-1}$, and $V_i=V(R_i)$. Select an unnormalized tangent by\n\n$$\\tau_i=\\begin{cases}\\Delta_i^+,&V_{i+1}>V_i>V_{i-1},\\\\\\Delta_i^-,&V_{i+1}<V_i<V_{i-1},\\\\w_{\\max}\\Delta_i^+ + w_{\\min}\\Delta_i^-,&\\text{otherwise and }V_{i+1}>V_{i-1},\\\\w_{\\min}\\Delta_i^+ + w_{\\max}\\Delta_i^-,&\\text{otherwise and }V_{i+1}<V_{i-1},\\\\\\Delta_i^++\\Delta_i^-,&V_{i+1}=V_{i-1},\\end{cases}$$\n\nwhere $w_{\\max}=\\max(|V_{i+1}-V_i|,|V_{i-1}-V_i|)$ and $w_{\\min}=\\min(|V_{i+1}-V_i|,|V_{i-1}-V_i|)$. If $\\tau_i=0$, return `tangent-failure`; otherwise set $t_i=\\tau_i/\\|\\tau_i\\|_2$. Nonfinite energies, gradients, or forces return `nonfinite-evaluation`.\n\nInitialize the update counter $k=0$. At iteration $k$, use the ordinary force\n\n$$F_i=-(I-t_it_i^T)\\nabla V(R_i)+\\kappa(\\|\\Delta_i^+\\|_2-\\|\\Delta_i^-\\|_2)t_i.$$\n\nWhen $k\\ge n_{\\rm climb}$, choose the least index $i_*$ attaining the largest interior energy and replace that image's force by\n\n$$F_{i_*}^{\\rm CI}=-\\nabla V(R_{i_*})+2(\\nabla V(R_{i_*})^Tt_{i_*})t_{i_*};$$\n\nthe climbing image has no spring force. The remaining interior images retain the ordinary force. Thus iterations $k=0,\\ldots,n_{\\rm climb}-1$ use ordinary forces and the first climbing force is evaluated at iteration $k=n_{\\rm climb}$. At each iteration report the maximum force norm and spacing residual $\\max_i|\\|\\Delta_i^+\\|_2-\\|\\Delta_i^-\\|_2|$. Stop with `tolerances-met` only if both are within their declared tolerances. If a tolerance fails and $k=N$, return `budget-exhausted`; only when $k<N$ update every interior image by $R_i^{k+1}=R_i^k+\\eta F_i^k$. Leaving $U$ returns `geometry-failure`. After a valid update set $k\\leftarrow k+1$ and repeat. The tolerance check precedes the budget check, so $N=0$ still checks the initial chain and $n_{\\rm climb}=N$ uses a climbing force at the final residual check (without an update if the budget is then exhausted).\n\nThe finite stopping status does not assert convergence to a MEP, a saddle, or a continuum path.",
